  "notes": "Two-storey ochre stucco corner shop at 5th: dark red ground band, green canvas awning, punched upper windows, a glazed corner bay. Folsom face: gated door, one upper window, a round window. Corner reads white stucco with a pitched (hipped) tower over the corner bay; the red band stops at 3.3 m (red only on the lower band). The white corner shop keeps a flat parapet (no hip across it); the pitched volume behind the corner is a grey block with a dark hipped cap; the long yellow part carries its own dark pitched roof with eaves, the red bays stay as its cross-gable fronts. Heights stay inside the LiDAR allowance. Less candy - muted ochre and brick red, grime and soot; the red base band runs the whole front (red bulkheads, narrower dark shop windows with more red wall between); one long dark-green awning from the corner shop across the adjacent frontage; a small dark gable over the corner (white walls, dark hip) instead of the grey block; reflection-dominant dark shop glass (glassModel). Shop glass dark tinted (glass-dark) instead of storefront glass that mirrored the warm horizon as beige boards; awnings 1.5 m deep; red wall zones under the red bays so the bays rise from the red base instead of floating. Corner block and bay bright white; awnings carry a 0.7 m green valance (awningSpans.valanceM) so they read as a band. Edge-3 wall override in a warm pale yellow on painted-white. Walls must top out at the LiDAR height and anything above may rise only 0.6 m (verify:blender-buildings); a gable needs a gate/owner decision. Edge 3 pale yellow toned down to #e8dbb4. Upper floor cream (#efe6cf) over a darker, less saturated red base (#6a2b27). Folsom-face shop glass dark opaque reflective. Upper glass opaque dark reflective too.",
